<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  EXAMPLE ONLY - not installed. Installing it is the operator's call.

  D1 sleeve executor (Sleeve S1 on the d1-sleeve Hyperliquid sub-account).
  As written it has NO arming flags, so every hourly run is a DRY RUN: it
  never loads the private key, never imports the signing SDK, builds no
  exchange client, writes nothing and logs signing_client=none
  exchange_posts=0. Adding the two arming strings (enabled and
  i-accept-live-risk, each with the usual two-dash prefix) to
  ProgramArguments right after the approval path is Albert's explicit
  arming act; nothing else arms it. (XML comments cannot contain a double
  hyphen, so no flag is spelled here.)

  Design: one idempotent run per hour at minute 15. Each run re-reads the
  venue, resolves any ambiguous order, makes every owned position hold
  exactly one verified reduce-only stop, closes positions whose virtual
  trade closed in the shadow ledger, then takes today's fresh shadow
  entries (within 6 hours of 00:00 UTC). A re-run on the same UTC day that
  finds nothing to do makes no mutation. A missed hour is caught up by the
  next one.

  Minute 15 is clear of the quiet window (minutes 57 to 03, when the
  executor makes no Hyperliquid call) and follows the shadow's own run.
  launchd StartCalendarInterval uses local time, but only Minute is set, so
  the job runs at :15 of every hour in any time zone.

  Credentials come from ~/.config/hypervector/d1_sleeve.env, outside the
  repository, owned by this user with mode 0600 (chmod 600). It holds the
  sleeve API wallet key and address, the sub-account address and the
  master address, never the engine key (a file naming the engine key is
  refused). No EnvironmentVariables are set here on purpose.

  launchd does not create the log directory: create data/runtime/d1_sleeve
  (and data/live/d1_sleeve) before bootstrapping, or the job cannot start.

  Pause: touch data/live/d1_sleeve/STOP. STOP means reduce-only mode (no
  entries, no leverage changes); exits, stop repair and breach closes
  continue. A STOP touched during a run blocks that run's remaining entries.
  Off: launchctl bootout of this label, in this order: touch STOP, wait for
  the current run's summary line in the log, then bootout. A bootout during
  the entry phase can stop the process between a fill and its stop, and no
  hourly run follows a bootout, so after ANY bootout run the status command
  with its venue flag; one armed run (or flatten) re-places or closes a
  position left without a stop.

  Armed runs refused before they start (torn journal, an approval that no
  longer pins the code, env file drift) raise a critical banner, an
  alerts.jsonl record and, when the env loads, the webhook; the dead-man URL
  is pinged only by runs that finish. Armed runs also take a host-wide lock,
  ~/.config/hypervector/d1_sleeve.SUBFP.lock (SUBFP = the sub-account
  fingerprint), so a second checkout can never trade the same sub-account
  at the same time.

  Operator prerequisites: approve the sleeve API wallet on the master under
  the exact name d1-sleeve (approving it under an existing name such as
  hl-api replaces the engine's signer); set a new sub-account's abstraction
  to unifiedAccount or disabled (a new sub reports default, which probe
  refuses); keep the host clock NTP-synced (an ambiguous order is resolved
  5 s after its expiry, so a run whose clock is more than 3 s from the
  venue's Date header takes no entries and raises critical clock_skew).

  A technical failure or an unprotected position in a run halts that run's
  remaining entries (never exits or stop repair); nothing is skipped, so
  the next hourly run retries them inside the 6 h window. A stop that
  vanished while its position was open is critical (stop_missing) and is
  re-placed. The canary waits about a minute after its stop rests to prove
  the stop outlives its expiresAfter: start it before minute 40.

  Python runs isolated (-I): PYTHONPATH, user site-packages and the script
  directory are not on the import path; the executor appends its own
  directory to import the shadow runner and its core.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<key>ExitTimeOut</key>
	<integer>60</integer>
	<key>Label</key>
	<string>local.hypervector.sleeve.d1_executor</string>
	<key>ProcessType</key>
	<string>Standard</string>
	<key>ProgramArguments</key>
	<array>
		<string>/Users/gestas/Prototypes/hypervector/.venv/bin/python</string>
		<string>-I</string>
		<string>-u</string>
		<string>/Users/gestas/Prototypes/hypervector/scripts/d1_sleeve_executor.py</string>
		<string>run</string>
		<string>--approval</string>
		<string>/Users/gestas/Prototypes/hypervector/docs/live-approvals/d1-sleeve-v1-YYYYMMDD.json</string>
	</array>
	<key>RunAtLoad</key>
	<false/>
	<key>StandardErrorPath</key>
	<string>/Users/gestas/Prototypes/hypervector/data/runtime/d1_sleeve/executor.log</string>
	<key>StandardOutPath</key>
	<string>/Users/gestas/Prototypes/hypervector/data/runtime/d1_sleeve/executor.log</string>
	<key>StartCalendarInterval</key>
	<dict>
		<key>Minute</key>
		<integer>15</integer>
	</dict>
	<key>WorkingDirectory</key>
	<string>/Users/gestas/Prototypes/hypervector</string>
</dict>
</plist>
